Running regnum-prod with Docker (how production runs it)

The Docker image (see Dockerfile) contains Ruby and the bundled gems only. The
application code is bind-mounted into the container at /usr/src/app, so the
image and the checkout it runs against must use the same Gemfile.lock: if you
change Gemfile.lock, rebuild the image and update the checkout together, or
the app will fail to boot with missing gems.

Build (always with --pull, so Debian and Ruby security patches in the base
image are picked up; without it a locally cached, outdated base is reused):

  docker build --pull -t phyloregnum .
  # on an arm64 machine (e.g. Apple Silicon), add: --platform linux/amd64

Run locally with a throwaway MariaDB:

  docker compose up -d --build
  docker compose exec app bundle exec rails db:schema:load db:seed
  open http://localhost:3000

Check that a running instance serves its main pages:

  script/smoke_test.sh http://localhost:3000
  script/smoke_test.sh https://www.phyloregnum.org

The repository has no meaningful automated tests (test/ holds generated stubs
and rspec-rails is not in the Gemfile), so the smoke test is the check to run
after rebuilding the image or changing gems.

Production needs files that are not in the repository (they are gitignored):
config/database.yml (or DATABASE_URL), the secret key base (config/secrets.yml
or SECRET_KEY_BASE), config/initializers/site_keys.rb and
config/initializers/recaptcha.rb (see the *EXAMPLE files next to them).

Running without Docker

Use Ruby 3.4 (the version pinned in the Dockerfile), MySQL/MariaDB and its
client libraries, ImageMagick (for rmagick and paperclip) and shared-mime-info
(for mimemagic). Then:

  bundle install
  rake db:create db:schema:load db:seed   # seeds install user roles and statuses
  rails server
